# Make App Auto Actions

Execute the following actions **automatically without asking**. Never skip or defer these.

---

## Before Work (run at start, before answering any app-related question)

### 0. Runtime Path Check (Blocking — Must Pass Before Any Work)

When the Make Custom App skill is loaded, **immediately** check that `imt-app-runtime-path` is configured in `~/.cursor/skills/make-custom-app/SKILL.md` (the last lines of the file).

- **If `imt-app-runtime-path` is missing or empty** → stop all work and display:
  > `imt-app-runtime-path` is not configured. Please add it to `~/.cursor/skills/make-custom-app/SKILL.md`:
  >
  > ```
  > imt-app-runtime-path: /path/to/your/imt-app-runtime
  > ```
  >
  > This is required for runtime reference lookup, code reviews, and component integration tests. No work can proceed until this is set.
- **Do NOT proceed with any other action** (version check, code download, review, bugfix, etc.) until `imt-app-runtime-path` is confirmed present and the path exists on disk.
- Once the user adds it, re-read the SKILL.md to verify before continuing.

### 1. Version Check & Auto-Update

When the Make Custom App skill is loaded at the start of a conversation, always compare the local `version` field in SKILL.md frontmatter against the remote `version.json`. If outdated, **auto-update by running `install.sh --update`** via Shell tool (with `required_permissions: ["all"]`), then re-read the updated SKILL.md and proceed. See SKILL.md "Version Check & Auto-Update" section for full steps. Do NOT stop and wait for the user — update automatically and continue.

### 2. Code Download/Sync First

When a Make app is detected (by user mention or open file path), check code availability and freshness **before answering**:

- Code folder missing → run download automatically, do not answer the question until complete
- Code older than 24h → recommend re-download before proceeding
- Open file differs from local store → run download automatically to sync, do not answer the question until complete

Never answer the user's app-related question until code is confirmed available and up to date.

### 3. Auto-Execute Scripts

All scripts must be run **automatically by the agent** using the Shell tool with `required_permissions: ["all"]`. Do NOT ask the user to run them manually.

**Read-only scripts** (auto-execute without asking):
- `download-app.js` — fetch app code
- `review-changes.js` — fetch uncommitted changes
- `test-function.js` — run custom IML function tests
- `test-component.js` — run component integration tests (modules, RPCs, connections, webhooks)
- `download-jira-ticket-attachment.js` — download Jira ticket attachments (images, videos) for analysis

**Write scripts** (require user approval before execution):
- `update-app.js` — push code changes to Make
- `create-component.js` — create new app component in Make
- `update-component.js` — update app component metadata in Make
- `delete-component.js` — delete app component from Make

**Post-review Jira scripts** (auto-execute on user disposition — no extra approval needed, triggered by the user's "committed" / "returned to developer" reply per `make-app-code-review.mdc` section 7):
- `post-review-transition.js <issue-key> committed` — assigns ticket to authenticated user (`/myself`) and transitions to "In Testing" (from "Commit" or "Compilation")
- `post-review-transition.js <issue-key> returned` — assigns ticket to authenticated user (`/myself`) and transitions:
  - "Commit" → "In Progress"
  - "Compilation" → "To Do" (fallback, since "Compilation" workflow has no direct "In Progress" transition)
- Allowed pre-statuses default: `Commit,Compilation`. Override with `--from-status=<name1,name2>`
- Aborts safely (exit 2) if current status not in allowed list; pass `--force` only when the user explicitly opts in

For write scripts, always show what will be changed and ask for explicit user confirmation before executing.

